 172: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
 173:     """Predict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.
 174: 
 175:     Input structure
 176:     - The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.
 177:     - The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.
 178:     - Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.
 179: 
 180:     Rule
 181:     - Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.
 182:     - For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.
 183:     - Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.
 184: 
 185:     Key insight
 186:     - The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.
 187:     """
